# Digest of Significant Case-Related Memoranda Issued by the Office for Civil Rights, January through December 1980, Volume 2.

**Authors:** 

## Abstract
This report summarizes memoranda issued by the Department of Education's Office for Civil Rights (OCR) to clarify policy applications of Title IX (Education Amendments of 1972), Title VI (Civil Rights Act of 1964), and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973. Cases discussed concern sex discrimination and equal opportunities in school athletics, scholarship awards, and vocational education; minority group employment in educational institutions; and placement and due process for handicapped students. (MJL)

